msgstr ""
"# Accuracy Comparison Example\n"
"\n"
"This document provides a detailed comparison of the accuracy of different translation methods, including rule-based machine translation (RBMT), statistical machine translation (SMT), and neural machine translation (NMT), along with human translation. The comparison is based on a set of standard test corpora and evaluation metrics such as BLEU, METEOR, and TER.\n"
"\n"
"## Test Setup\n"
"\n"
"- **Test Corpus**: A collection of 1,000 sentences covering various domains, including technology, medicine, law, and daily conversation.\n"
"- **Evaluation Metrics**: BLEU, METEOR, and TER scores are used to measure translation quality.\n"
"- **Translation Methods**: \n"
"  - RBMT (Rule-Based Machine Translation)\n"
"  - SMT (Statistical Machine Translation)\n"
"  - NMT (Neural Machine Translation)\n"
"  - Human Translation (as a benchmark)\n"
"\n"
"## Results\n"
"\n"
"The following table summarizes the average scores for each method across all test sentences:\n"
"\n"
"| Method | BLEU | METEOR | TER |\n"
"|--------|------|--------|-----|\n"
"| RBMT   | 0.35 | 0.52   | 0.68 |\n"
"| SMT    | 0.48 | 0.61   | 0.55 |\n"
"| NMT    | 0.62 | 0.74   | 0.41 |\n"
"| Human  | 0.85 | 0.92   | 0.15 |\n"
"\n"
"## Analysis\n"
"\n"
"1. **RBMT** relies on linguistic rules and dictionaries, performing well in specific domains but poorly in handling colloquial expressions and ambiguous sentences.\n"
"2. **SMT** improves translation quality by learning from large parallel corpora, but its performance is limited by the quality and size of the training data.\n"
"3. **NMT** uses deep learning models to capture contextual information, significantly improving fluency and accuracy, especially in handling long sentences and complex structures.\n"
"4. **Human Translation** remains the gold standard, but it is time-consuming and costly.\n"
"\n"
"## Conclusion\n"
"\n"
"Neural machine translation demonstrates the highest accuracy among automated methods, approaching human-level performance in many cases. However, for highly specialized or culturally sensitive content, human translation remains indispensable.\n"

